# Copy to .env.local.

# Base URL of the Tone Studio API.
#
# Leave it blank and the app still runs — takes stay session-local and simply
# cannot be persisted (see `isApiConfigured` in src/lib/api.ts). That is
# deliberate: the frontend must be runnable without a server.
#
# The value is inlined into the client bundle at build time, as every
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable is. Never put a secret here.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3100

# Claude API key, for the tone assistant's /api/tone route.
#
# Optional. Without it the assistant still works: the genre modes and the local
# Thai/English intent engine in src/lib/toneIntent.ts answer every request offline
# and for free, and the route returns 503 `no-key` so the client falls back
# silently. With it, requests go to Claude first and the fallback only catches
# failures.
#
# NOT prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_, and it must never be. Every NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable is
# inlined into the JavaScript sent to the browser — the property that makes the API
# URL above safe to expose is exactly what would publish this key to every visitor.
# It is read server-side only, inside the route handler.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
